# MySQL — Hostinger hPanel > Databases (free, included in the plan).
# For local dev: docker compose up -d  →  mysql://ftse:ftse@localhost:3306/ftse
DATABASE_URL=mysql://user:password@localhost:3306/ftse

# Outbound messaging — OPTIONAL. Leads are stored in MySQL first and the panel
# reads them from there, so the portal works with none of these set. A webhook
# adds outbound delivery: a copy of each lead pushed to whatever CRM you point
# it at (GoHighLevel, n8n, your own endpoint).
#
# The same endpoint also receives operator alerts — {"event":"operator_alert"}
# with kind "new_lead" or "review_submitted" — so a flow can forward "go look"
# to WhatsApp while routing {"event":"lead"} into the CRM. With no webhook set
# there is no alert: /admin badges the review queue and the last 24 h of leads,
# which needs no configuration at all.
LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Historical alias for LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL; either name works.
GHL_WEBHOOK_URL=
GHL_API_KEY=

# Outbound email — the buyer's and the lister's channel (src/lib/crm.ts).
#
# The one-time login code and every transactional message go out over SMTP,
# against a mailbox on the same Hostinger account the site deploys to (create
# it in hPanel > Emails; it can be the same mailbox as CONTACT_EMAIL below).
#
# LAUNCH BLOCKER, not a nice-to-have: without these, production OTP login and
# lead mail silently do not send. They are optional in development only — with
# none of them set, the console transport prints the message and reports
# success, which really is a delivery to the only recipient a laptop has. In
# production the same absence reports FAILURE and prints nothing, because a
# line claiming a code was sent when it was not is how a publisher gets told
# "check your inbox" for a message nobody could ever receive.
#
# All-or-nothing: a half-filled set (a host with no password, say) reads as no
# transport rather than throwing on the first send.
#
# Swapping SMTP for a transactional provider (Resend/Postmark) later is a class
# in crm.ts and these variables, not an architecture change.
SMTP_HOST=
# 587 = STARTTLS (the Hostinger default), 465 = implicit TLS. Optional.
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
# The From: address. Defaults to SMTP_USER when unset.
EMAIL_FROM=

# Cloudflare R2 — listing photos. Free tier: 10 GB, zero egress.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=ftse-images
# Public delivery URL for the bucket. Use the bucket's own public URL
# (https://pub-<hash>.r2.dev) or a custom domain YOU HAVE MAPPED in
# Cloudflare. Do NOT point this at a domain that isn't set up —
# Pointing it at a domain that is not actually mapped would 404 every photo
# the day R2 goes live (audit F64).
# Leave empty until the bucket exists: empty = stored keys pass through
# unchanged, which keeps imported remote-URL photos working.
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Portal contact identity (src/config/contact.ts) — footer, /contacto,
# privacy policy and Organization JSON-LD all read these. Both stay `string |
# null` in code with NO fallback: empty means the site shows no address and no
# WhatsApp CTA, routing everyone to the on-site lead form instead — never a
# compose window to a mailbox nobody owns.
#
# CONTACT_EMAIL is REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH. Sweden is email-first: a Swedish
# consumer portal with no email address on its contact page is not credible.
# That is a launch-checklist requirement, not a type change — fill it with a
# mailbox that is actually monitored (audit F10).
# CONTACT_WHATSAPP stays optional: it is the AGENCY-side channel here, not the
# buyer's — Spanish agencies live on WhatsApp, Swedish buyers do not.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means Next inlines them at BUILD time — a rebuild is required
# after changing either, not just a restart.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_WHATSAPP=

# Claude API — area guides + ES→SV listing translations (batch jobs, NEVER the
# request path). `npm run cron:translate` fills listings.title_sv/description_sv
# from the agency feed's Spanish; with no key it refuses to run rather than writing anything,
# and the site is unaffected — publishing never calls the API, so it cannot be
# blocked by one being down (src/lib/translate.ts explains why there is no
# publish-time hook).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: the model cron:translate uses. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
ANTHROPIC_TRANSLATION_MODEL=

# Canonical host (listing detail pages are canonical here only). One door
# today; do NOT point this at a domain that is not owned and does not have a
# `VERTICALS` entry — that resurrects broken canonicals sitewide
# (see src/config/verticals.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CANONICAL_HOST=flyttatillspanien.se

# How old the newest EUR/SEK rate may be before every kronor figure disappears
# from the site (src/lib/format.ts `formatSek`). The EUR price is unaffected: a
# missing SEK figure is a small disappointment, a confidently wrong one is a
# complaint. Optional — defaults to 7 when unset.
FX_MAX_AGE_DAYS=7
